[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Its own table shows two causes. The queued
parser fix closes one of them. The other keeps coming in after it ships.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

One ticket per row:

| problem | row | reports | ticket |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parser`: the shared parser reads day-first dates month first | `parser` | 379 | [#1](https://github.com/chillleader/mega-s01e03/issues/1) |
| `hint`: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field | `hint`, marked "no ticket of its own" | 33 | [#2](https://github.com/chillleader/mega-s01e03/issues/2) |

## How each report was placed

1. **Repeats out first.** The ticket export comes in overlapping pages, so one id can appear twice. One id, one report.
2. **By tenant, not by intake tag.** Every tenant on file writes the day first. A report that came through the
   booking form of a `booking-v3` tenant is `hint`: that form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Every other
   report is `parser`. The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser and disagrees often.

## Why it matters

- **parser** is the fix already queued. Ship it.
- **hint** survives that fix: the form tells people to type month first and then reads the date day first. Change the
  hint on `booking-v3` to the tenant's order.

## Open question

The note under the table: 5 `parser` reports read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), Tuesday shown as Monday,
12 May as 11 May. Day and month are not swapped there. They are counted in #1. If they keep coming after the parser
fix ships, look at time zones and DST where an invite's date is turned into a timestamp.

## Lessons

- A count of reports says nothing about how many problems they hold. 412 reports with 12 different subject lines
  went into one ticket, and every subject line carries reports of both causes.
- Count with the desk's own table. A ticket the desk cannot find a row for is a ticket it cannot match.

